# Autonomous production engineering (orchestrator)

Parent Agent = helper/orchestrator. For behavior changes, bugs, features, meaningful
refactors, API/persistence/infra changes — run this workflow automatically.
User does not need to name subagents.

Skip full pipeline for: Q&A, tiny docs/typo/format-only edits.

## Human finish line (mandatory)
Agents do engineering work through Final Verifier VERIFIED + local-gate green.
**Do NOT push, force-push, open/merge PRs, or deploy** unless the user explicitly says
to. Default end state: READY_FOR_HUMAN_PR. Human reviews and PR/pushes.

## 0. Scope lock (mandatory)
When the user names a folder/repo/path (e.g. `kafka`, `inventory/src/...`):
1. Set `TARGET_REPO` + `TARGET_PATH` from that request.
2. Read **that** tree first (code, tests, AGENTS.md, APIs).
3. Work **only** inside that scope unless a tiny documented cross-cut is required.
4. No unrelated features, pads, or drive-by cleanups.
5. Preserve backwards compatibility with existing callers/tests/schemas.

## Repo map
`kafka` | `redis` | `coding` | `inventory` | `orders` | `distributed-tracing` | `platform-ops`

Gates: `make -C platform-ops local-gate REPO=<name>` → `make anti-slop` (aislop ≥80).
Ship only when user asks.

## Edge-case matrix
`test-engineer` / `edge-case-breaker` / `final-verifier` share the matrix in
`edge-case-breaker.md`. Fix gaps before stopping.

## API documentation (automatic)
When the task creates/modifies/deletes an HTTP API or changes request/response/
auth/validation/status/side-effects, after fixes are stable invoke
**api-documentation-agent** so `docs/api/` matches FINAL code.
Also invoke it when the user manually asks to document a path.

## Agent communication
Every subagent call includes:

```
HANDOFF
TARGET_REPO:
TARGET_PATH:
User request:
Prior stage output:
Acceptance criteria:
Files in scope:
Out of scope:
Commands to run:
Findings so far:
```

## Stages
1. product-analyst
2. architect (if non-trivial)
3. implementer
4. test-engineer
5. Parallel: edge-case-breaker, security-reviewer, production-reviewer
6. Consolidate findings; auto-fix BLOCKER/CRITICAL/HIGH
7. Retest → re-review affected (max 3 cycles)
8. **api-documentation-agent** (if API touched, or user gave a docs path)
9. final-verifier (includes API doc freshness when APIs changed)
10. Stop for human — READY_FOR_HUMAN_PR. pr-integrator only if user asked to PR/push.

## Ask user ONLY when
- Material product ambiguity / missing credentials the agents cannot obtain locally
- Destructive production action without explicit auth
- Incompatible architecture with no project convention
- External system down with **no** local path
- **Before PR / push / deploy / force-push / merge** — human finish line

## Do NOT ask permission for (just run)
Local installs, tests, pytest/coverage, lint, ruff, scorecard, anti-slop, alembic
local, seed scripts, curl/health checks, reading code, editing in-scope files,
commits **when the user already asked to commit**. Only stop to ask for PR/push/ship.

## Quality scorecard (/100 — ship bar)
Run `make -C platform-ops scorecard` (excludes DSA coding). Dimensions each /100:
code_quality · open_source · seed_data · test_coverage · documentation ·
ai_slop (↑=better) · security · db_identity_indexes · optimal_code · production.
Target overall ≥ **80**; prefer ≥ **90** before human PR. Fix gaps in-scope.

## DB identity & indexes (when models/SQL exist)
- Every table needs a clear primary key / identity
- Hot query columns (FK, lookup, unique business keys) need indexes
- Migrations (Alembic) must match models; no silent drift
- Libraries without SQL: mark N/A in scorecard, do not invent schemas

## Optimal code (mandatory)
Prefer clear structure, typing, small modules, real error handling, reuse OSS
stack already in repo. Avoid padding, dead stubs, bare excepts, invented APIs.

## Production structure & size limits (mandatory)
- **Prod layout**: prefer `src/<package>/`, `tests/`, `docs/api/` (from real code),
  `alembic/` when persistence exists, thin handlers → services → models.
- **File size**: keep each source/doc file **≤ 600–1000 lines**. Split modules,
  routes, or docs before adding more. Never pad to fill the budget.
- **Commit size**: when the user asks to commit, create **one commit per logical
  unit**, with **≤ 500–700 lines added** (`git diff --cached --numstat` sum of
  insertions). Split agents/docs/code/tests into separate commits if needed.
- **Commit message**: clear conventional title + body (why, not only what).
  Example title: `docs(api): document kafka Flask routes from code`.
- Never commit secrets, `.env`, `vendor/`, `dist/`, or generated junk.

## Done (agent side)
Scoped behavior + AC + tests + no HIGH+ + reviews + API docs when APIs changed +
secrets clean + size limits respected + Final Verifier VERIFIED. Human then PR/pushes.

## Final user response
COMPLETED / Files / Validation / Edge matrix / API docs / READY_FOR_HUMAN_PR: yes
No transcripts. Never claim unrun commands or unsolicited PRs.
